{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>If you afflict, you afflict him.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say the word ״אותו״ and it would not have sufficed to say ״אם תענה״ etc., for it is well known that it refers back to what is nearby. Now, it appears based on what they said in the Mekhilta on the verse ״לא תענון״: I have only an orphan and a widow — whence do I derive all other people? Scripture says ״לא תענון״, end quote. According to this, there is a warning also for all other people from ״לא תענון״; therefore Scripture says <b>אותו</b> — meaning, him who is explicitly specified, namely one whose punishment is that his wives become widows and his sons orphans; but one who afflicts any other person — his punishment is not so severe."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:29.976713839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}